The report has been written to `docs/reviews/infrastructure/infra-07-docs-citation-verification.md`.

**Summary**: 14 findings across 4 severity levels:

- **4 High**: (1) EnergyPlus version references are inconsistent across 6 versions; (2) ASHRAE HOF edition drift — adjacent modules cite different editions of the same handbook; (3) EnergyPlus §-style section numbers are systematically unverifiable against the web-hosted Engineering Reference (~15+ distinct invalid § numbers); (4) OCHRE has no publication provenance — no paper, report, or version cited despite being the primary reference oracle.

- **7 Medium**: (5) Cutler et al. 2013 citation has 3 independent bibliographic errors; (6) Winkler thesis year misattributed as 2011 instead of 2009 in multiple docs; (7) Berdahl-Martin sky emissivity fix is incomplete — still missing Li et al. 2017 citation; (8) Multiple ASHRAE chapter numbers are wrong for the claimed edition; (9) BESTEST/ASHRAE 140-2017 reference bands lack version verification and access instructions; (10) NREL ResStock dataset has no version or access documentation; (11) `thermal-envelope-solver.md` claims Crank-Nicolson discretization but the code uses ZOH.

- **3 Low**: (12) Burch-Christensen model applicability range undocumented; (13) `ashrae_wind_stack()` function name conflates AIM-2 with Sherman-Grimsrud; (14) Validation data sources lack version numbers and URLs.
